228
00:19:36,830 --> 00:19:42,820
if you go over the point x, so
if you go from xn to x and then

229
00:19:42,820 --> 00:19:46,480
from x to xm like that.

230
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:54,400
But each of these, because
both of these, both little m

231
00:19:54,400 --> 00:19:57,260
and little n are
bigger than capital N,

232
00:19:57,260 --> 00:20:03,010
then both of these distances
are bounded by epsilon over 2.

233
00:20:03,010 --> 00:20:07,340
And so you see that this thing
here is smaller than epsilon.

234
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:10,120
So this proved that
in a metric space,

235
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:14,470
any convergent sequence
is also a Cauchy sequence.

236
00:20:14,470 --> 00:20:21,670
And so we know that
if the metric space is

237
00:20:21,670 --> 00:20:26,550
R with the usual
Euclidean distance,

238
00:20:26,550 --> 00:20:30,300
then actually, you
also-- and that

239
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:33,005
was the convergence
theorem, so the Cauchy.

240
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:36,755
convergence theorem.

241
00:20:41,310 --> 00:20:51,840
So Cauchy convergence theorem--
it said that if x comma d is R

242
00:20:51,840 --> 00:20:56,580
with the Euclidean distance-- so
I denote the Euclidean distance

243
00:20:56,580 --> 00:20:59,340
like this--

244
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:02,750
then we have the converse.

245
00:21:11,550 --> 00:21:14,222
So i.e.

246
00:21:14,222 --> 00:21:18,520
that any Cauchy sequence--

247
00:21:24,130 --> 00:21:27,320
