641
00:54:15,310 --> 00:54:18,430
Then this thing here is open.

642
00:54:18,430 --> 00:54:25,030
Any metric ball like
this is an open subset.

643
00:54:25,030 --> 00:54:26,480
Let's try to prove that.

644
00:54:26,480 --> 00:54:28,300
And again, whether
you're proving things

645
00:54:28,300 --> 00:54:32,410
like this for a metric space,
the only nontrivial thing

646
00:54:32,410 --> 00:54:34,250
is the triangle inequality.

647
00:54:34,250 --> 00:54:37,870
So this is relying on
the triangle inequality.

648
00:54:37,870 --> 00:54:41,890
And so for a lot of
things, when you're

649
00:54:41,890 --> 00:54:44,540
proving things about
a metric space,

650
00:54:44,540 --> 00:54:49,840
it's often quite helpful
to draw a little picture.

651
00:54:49,840 --> 00:54:54,370
But of course, you have
to be careful with, again,

652
00:54:54,370 --> 00:54:59,170
then the intuition
comes from Rn.

653
00:54:59,170 --> 00:55:03,940
And sometimes, the metric is
a little bit more complicated

654
00:55:03,940 --> 00:55:04,840
than that.

655
00:55:04,840 --> 00:55:10,730
So this here, imagine that
this is the ball of radius r.

656
00:55:10,730 --> 00:55:13,480
Here you have some x.

657
00:55:13,480 --> 00:55:17,000
Now take an element y.

658
00:55:17,000 --> 00:55:22,700
So suppose that y here
is now in this ball here.

659
00:55:22,700 --> 00:55:33,860
Then we want to show
that there exists

660
00:55:33,860 --> 00:55:42,620
that for some s bigger than
0, the ball here of radius

661
00:55:42,620 --> 00:55:48,530
s around y is now contained
in this ball here.

662
00:55:48,530 --> 00:55:50,940
So here, you have y.

663
00:55:50,940 --> 00:55:52,760
And we want to
prove that there is

664
00:55:52,760 --> 00:55:59,570
some little ball
around y that is

665
00:55:59,570 --> 00:56:02,270
contained in the original ball.

666
00:56:02,270 --> 00:56:08,690
And so, again, this is going to
rely on the triangle inequality.

667
00:56:08,690 --> 00:56:11,760
So you have y here.

668
00:56:11,760 --> 00:56:14,620
y was supposed to be
in this ball here.

669
00:56:14,620 --> 00:56:19,780
This means that the
distance from x to y

670
00:56:19,780 --> 00:56:23,620
is strictly the s in r.

671
00:56:23,620 --> 00:56:31,600
You take now s here to be
r minus this distance here.

672
00:56:31,600 --> 00:56:34,000
Why do I do this?

673
00:56:34,000 --> 00:56:36,910
In my picture here,
I have here x.

674
00:56:36,910 --> 00:56:39,250
I have here y.

675
00:56:39,250 --> 00:56:46,840
And our intuition is that if we
go from x and we go through y

676
00:56:46,840 --> 00:56:49,300
