to the boundary,

677
00:56:49,300 --> 00:56:55,160
then this thing
here is dx comma y.

678
00:56:55,160 --> 00:57:01,700
And this one here is r minus d.

679
00:57:01,700 --> 00:57:04,870
This is the remaining--
this whole here is r.

680
00:57:04,870 --> 00:57:07,100
This is dx comma y.

681
00:57:07,100 --> 00:57:10,750
So this here must be this here.

682
00:57:10,750 --> 00:57:14,330
And so if you're
setting this equal to s,

683
00:57:14,330 --> 00:57:18,260
and now you imagine taking
a ball here, well, then

684
00:57:18,260 --> 00:57:20,960
at least on the
picture, this whole ball

685
00:57:20,960 --> 00:57:23,240
is contained in
the original ball.

686
00:57:23,240 --> 00:57:27,390
So let's try to
see if that works.

687
00:57:27,390 --> 00:57:29,900
If that works, then
it really only used

688
00:57:29,900 --> 00:57:32,180
the triangle inequality.

689
00:57:32,180 --> 00:57:34,770
So we're setting
s equal to this.

690
00:57:34,770 --> 00:57:39,900
And then we're looking at
this ball here around S.

691
00:57:39,900 --> 00:57:44,130
And we take an element
here in this ball.

692
00:57:44,130 --> 00:57:46,260
And we now need to prove--

693
00:57:46,260 --> 00:57:47,650
so we need to show.

694
00:57:53,210 --> 00:57:55,640
We want to prove that
this whole ball is

695
00:57:55,640 --> 00:57:57,150
contained in the original ball.

696
00:57:57,150 --> 00:58:01,160
So this means that we need to
prove that for any such element

697
00:58:01,160 --> 00:58:06,170
set here is in this thing here.

698
00:58:06,170 --> 00:58:07,600
That's what we need to prove.

699
00:58:14,220 --> 00:58:16,025
And so now you see--

700
00:58:23,590 --> 00:58:26,650
so we take z.

